nodecode-omonpakari is a rewrite of tamamo510's tamamo510/omonpakari:
  https://github.com/tamamo510/omonpakari
  commit 8da1d8ab1a45de362c2491146f0946e8b4467045
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 tamamo510 (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the seven tools, the reference table of absorption
interactions with its sources, the cycle arithmetic that answers a window of
dates rather than a single day, the life notes, the composed states and the
pressure reading with its level and trend, and above all the pre_llm_call
hook: before each reply a short quiet picture of today is added to the
standing context, so suggestions are weighed against the person's body and
habits first. The original keeps its journal in the host's SQLite plugin
database; this rewrite keeps the same journal, marks, notes and pressure
samples in one JSON file under the organism's home, through no database
driver. What was left out: the background hourly pressure refresh thread and
the cron-turn switch (a Nodecode turn is a turn the person started), the
duplicate detection that dropped a repeated note from a conversation, and the
per-medication count limits are kept but not surfaced in the picture. Nothing
of the original's code runs: it is Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell
contract, and OpenWeather is the one host it speaks to.
